# {{PROJECT_TITLE}} — project rules (always on)

This folder is a **Project**: one investigation into {{PHYSICAL_SYSTEM}}, hosting many **campaigns** (versioned
attempts) and **sessions** (ad-hoc work). These rules bind every agent working anywhere under this tree. Read
`PROJECT.md` for the goal and `LINEAGE.md` for what has been done. (Each campaign also has its own `CLAUDE.md`
with the loop spine; this file adds the project-level rules on top.)

## Structure
`Project → Campaign → Experiment` (+ ad-hoc `sessions/`). Campaigns live in `campaigns/<name>/`; ad-hoc work in
`sessions/<YYYY-MM-DD>_<slug>/`; shared data/docs at the project root; one `reports/`.

## Non-negotiable rules
1. **Shared data is referenced, never copied.** Use `../../data` and `../../shared` (relative). **Never copy the
   data into a campaign, never write into `data/`.** Copied data is what breaks paths — don't create it.
2. **Everything is indexed in `LINEAGE.md`.** A campaign gets a row; a session gets a row; a within-campaign
   version bump gets a one-line change-record. Nothing significant happens off the ledger.
3. **Campaign vs session.** One optimizable **frozen metric driving a loop** → a **campaign** (`new-campaign`).
   Exploration / debugging / a one-off analysis with no frozen metric → a **session** (a `sessions/<…>/` folder
   with a `NOTES.md`). When unsure, start a session; promote later.
4. **Findings at their true tier.** A session finding, or an unverified result, is recorded as such — it is
   **not** a verified DISCOVERY unless it passed `verify`. Do not let ad-hoc conclusions be trusted like
   campaign results.
5. **Invalidating updates fork-and-archive — they do not silently carry forward.** If a change (e.g. a fixed
   forward-model bug, a corrected dataset) **invalidates or makes misleading** a campaign's prior findings,
   **fork a fresh-ledger campaign and archive the old one** (`campaigns/_archive/`, frozen, still in LINEAGE).
   The old `results/`/`JOURNAL` do NOT become the new effort's working documents; carry forward only findings
   that survive **re-verification**, with provenance. A journal built on a known-bad model must never steer the
   next effort silently.
6. **Consumed artifacts come from `shared/`.** If a sibling campaign froze something you depend on (a forward
   model, a training set), reference the **promoted** copy in `../../shared/`, not the sibling's working folder;
   and declare the FROZEN/MUTABLE relationship in your campaign's `charter.md`.

## Portability
All internal references are relative; the whole `<project>/` tree relocates as one unit. The only absolute path
is the resolved `data_path` (in `PROJECT.md`) when the canonical data lives off-tree.
